# Built assets. Vite writes LF, but core.autocrlf=true is set on this machine,
# so git wants CRLF in the working tree and flags every file under dist/ as
# modified after a build even when the bytes are identical to what is committed.
# `git diff` then shows nothing, because it normalises - so the noise hides real
# changes rather than reporting them.
#
# Pinning these to LF makes the working tree match what the build actually
# produces. Scoped to dist/ deliberately: a repo-wide `* text=auto` would
# renormalise thousands of existing files in one go.
dist/** text eol=lf
